REASONING: The Uigur Khaganate established Ordu-Baliq as its capital, an extensive city featuring a royal palace and fortifications, directly evidencing Level 1. Archaeological surveys and historical accounts also indicate the presence of smaller fortified towns and administrative centers (Level 2) throughout their domain, alongside widespread basic settlements and nomadic encampments (Level 3) associated with their semi-nomadic lifestyle and control over vast territories.
Levels present: {1,2,3}
